cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "INVARIANT: a quant research pipeline that tries to kill every candidate signal"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Raut
    given-names: Om
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/omraut888/invariant"
url: "https://github.com/omraut888/invariant"
abstract: >-
  A research pipeline that puts candidate trading signals through a causal screen, a decay
  test and portfolio construction, records every kill in a hash-chained ledger, and writes a
  verified template memo. Each stage was validated on a planted-signal benchmark by a
  pre-registered study before use on real data.
keywords:
  - quantitative finance
  - causal discovery
  - multiple testing
  - reproducibility
